course: dictionary
lesson: 2401
title: Curvy means bendy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Curvy is an adjective, so it describes a thing. It can change form: curvy, curvier, curviest. Its everyday meaning is simple: a curvy thing has many curves or bends, and it is not straight. «The curvy road wound up the hill like a snake.» The road is not straight, so curvy means bendy.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Dad slowed the car for every curvy bend.» Slowing down for bends tells you the road turns a lot. Ask yourself what would fit here. Straight would not fit, so curvy must mean the opposite of straight. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In maths and art, the usual school word is curved, as in «a curved line». Curvy is more casual, the kind of word you might use when talking about a river or a path. Use curved in your writing at school, and you can understand curvy when you hear it.
explain: Some grown-ups also use curvy to describe a person's body. That is an informal, adult use, and you do not need to use it yourself. When you meet a word in a new way, the clues around it show you the meaning, and the clear meaning here is bendy, not straight.
fact: Curvy means having many curves or bends, not straight.
fact: «The river was curvy, looping round every field.» Here curvy describes the shape of the river.
fact: Curvy changes form: curvy, curvier, curviest.
fact: Curved is the usual word in maths lessons; curvy is more casual.
fact: Some grown-ups use curvy about a person's body. This is an informal, adult use, so you do not need to use it yourself.
exercise: «The curvy road wound up the hill.» What does curvy mean here? | Wet and muddy | Very fast and flat | Bright red in colour | *Having many bends, not straight
exercise: Which word is the usual maths word for a bendy line? | *curved | flat | thin | straight
exercise: «Dad slowed down for every curvy bend.» Which word is the opposite of curvy? | loud | round | *straight | bendy
test: Find and copy the word that describes a line that bends: «The curvy line looped across the page.» | page | across | line | *curvy
test: Which word is the next step up from curvy, for a road that is even more bendy? | *curvier | curved | curvy | straight
exam: A ruler is straight, but a garden hose lying on the grass is usually | *curvy | straight | heavy | cold
